"""mad - the MAD Terminal.

Grade before you sign. MAD talks back: every output is the angry
auditor, not a neutral help text. Verdicts land like MAD lands them;
errors talk back too. The facts are exact - the voice wraps them,
never replaces them.

Free doors first, always. The paid doors (check/*, witness) cost
0.01 USDC via x402 on Base - this CLI NEVER pays. On a 402 it prints
the bill and exits with the 402 facts. Pass a payload you signed
elsewhere with --payment and it will resend it; mad never signs.
Read-only on chain. No wallet actions, no gas, no spending.

    mad                 interactive mode (plain English, MAD answers)
    mad test            the free look - grade yourself
    mad check agent 1224530
    mad seal 0x...      is this token sealed?
    mad mcp             hand the MCP server to Claude / Codex / Grok
    mad fix             re-grade a FAIL and print the fix - apply the
                        safe ones only when you say yes
Bare `mad` wakes MAD up: it shows what moved since your last run
(witness seq, dust, freshest grade) and the next check worth your
time. Every verdict travels three lanes - the API door live, a
pre-computed lane, and the chained witness ledger.
And `mad` talks: the REPL is a conversation, not a command line.
Ask in plain English, MAD answers in its own voice, and it remembers
what you graded, asked, and answered - session memory in the same
state file, yours to delete. `history` shows the conversation,
`forget` wipes it.
